*Proof:* Consider the triple  $(4^n, 4^{2n-1}-1, 4^{2n-1}+1)$ . It is easy to see that   $$ (4^n)^2+(4^{2n-1}-1)^2=4^{2n}+4^{4n-2}+1-2\cdot4^{2n-1}=4^{4n-2}+2\cdot4^{2n-1}=(4^{2n-1}+1)^2.\ \blacksquare $$  Now, consider the parabolic triangle determined by the points  $(4^n, 16^n), (-4^n, 16^n), \left(4^{2n-1}+1, (4^{2n-1}+1)^2\right)$  for  $n\in \mathbb{N}$ .
