The area of this triangle is   $$ \frac{1}{2}\left(2\cdot4^n\right)\left((4^{2n-1}+1)^2-16^n\right)=4^n\cdot \left(4^{2n-1}-1\right)^2=\left(2^n\cdot(4^{2n-1}-1)\right)^2, $$  and  $4^{2n-1}-1$  is clearly odd. This shows that for all  $n\ge 1$  there is a parabolic triangle with area  $(2^nm)^2$ . The only thing left is  $n=0$ , which is trivial: consider the triangle with vertices  $(-1,1),(0,0),(1,1)$ .</details>

