My solution:
<details><summary>hide because length</summary>I claim that  $3\cdot 7\cdot 11\cdots 4019$  is the maximum, from the conditions  $a_1a_2\le 3$ ,  $a_3a_4\le 7$ , etc. Now we must prove this is attainable.

First, I will prove that there exists  $a_1, a_2, \ldots , a_{2010}$  such that  $a_ia_j > i+j$  if and only if  $|i-j|=1$ .

Choose  $a_k=\sqrt{2k+\dfrac{1}{2k}}$ . Then   $$ a_ia_j=\sqrt{2i+\dfrac{1}{2i}}\cdot \sqrt{2j+\dfrac{1}{2j}}=\sqrt{4ij+\dfrac{i}{j}+\dfrac{j}{i}+\dfrac{1}{4ij}} \stackrel{?}{>}i+j=\sqrt{4ij+(i-j)^2} $$    $$ \implies \dfrac{i}{j}+\dfrac{j}{i}+\dfrac{1}{4ij}\stackrel{?}{>}(i-j)^2\implies i^2+j^2+\dfrac{1}{4} \stackrel{?}{>}ij(i-j)^2 $$  Now WLOG  $i>j$  and let  $i=j+d$ . Then   $$ i^2+j^2+\dfrac{1}{4} \stackrel{?}{>}ij(i-j)^2\implies (j+d)^2+j^2+\dfrac{1}{4} \stackrel{?}{>} d^2j(j+d)\implies 2j^2+2jd+d^2+\dfrac{1}{4}\stackrel{?}{>}j^2d^2+jd^3\implies (d^2-2)j^2+(d^3-2d)j\stackrel{?}{<}d^2+\dfrac{1}{4} $$  If  $|i-j|=1\implies d=1$  then clearly the inequality is true, so the if direction is proved. Otherwise  $d\ge 2$  and we want to prove   $$ (d^2-2)j^2+(d^3-2d)j\stackrel{?}{\ge}d^2+\dfrac{1}{4} $$   However,  $(d^2-2)j^2+(d^3-2d)j\ge (d^2-2)+(d^3-2d)=d^3+d^2-2d-2$  so it remains to show   $$ d^3+d^2-2d-2\stackrel{?}{\ge} d^2+\dfrac{1}{4}\implies d^3-2d-\dfrac{9}{4}\stackrel{?}{\ge}0 $$   which is clearly true if  $d\ge 2$ .

Now we have to fudge the number around so that  $a_ia_{i+1}>(i)+(i+1)$  if and only if  $i$  is odd. Note that we can decrease some of the  $a_k$  as we wish without disturbing  $a_ia_j \le i+j$  if  $|i-j|\ge 2$  because it only decreases the LHS. Thus, I choose to let  $a_k=\sqrt{2k+\dfrac{1}{2k}}$  if  $k$  is odd, and  $a_k=\sqrt{2k+\dfrac{m_k}{k}}$  for some constant  $m_k\le \dfrac{1}{2}$  dependent on  $k$  if  $k$  is even. Thus we want  $a_{2k-1}a_{2k} > 4k-1$  but  $a_{2k}a_{2k+1} < 4k+1$ . Substituting, we need   $$ \left\{
\begin{array}{l}
\sqrt{4k-2+\dfrac{1}{4k-2}}\cdot \sqrt{4k+\dfrac{m_k}{2k}} > 4k-1
\sqrt{4k+2-\dfrac{1}{4k+2}}\cdot \sqrt{4k+\dfrac{m_k}{2k}} < 4k+1
\end{array}
\right.
\implies
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
\left(4k-2+\dfrac{1}{4k-2}\right)\left( 4k+\dfrac{m_k}{2k}\right) > (4k-1)^2
\left(4k+2+\dfrac{1}{4k+2}\right)\left( 4k+\dfrac{m_k}{2k}\right)< (4k+1)^2
\end{array}
\right. $$    $$ \implies \left\{
\begin{array}{l}
16k^2-8k+\dfrac{4k}{4k-2}+2m_k-\dfrac{m_k}{k}+\dfrac{m_k}{2k(4k-2)} > 16k^2-8k+1
16k^2+8k+\dfrac{4k}{4k-2}+2m_k+\dfrac{m_k}{k}+\dfrac{m_k}{2k(4k-2)} < 16k^2+8k+1
\end{array}
\right.
\implies \left\{
\begin{array}{l}
\dfrac{4k}{4k-2}+2m_k-\dfrac{m_k}{k}+\dfrac{m_k}{2k(4k-2)} > 1
\dfrac{4k}{4k-2}+2m_k+\dfrac{m_k}{k}+\dfrac{m_k}{2k(4k-2)} < 1
\end{array}
\right. $$  Now we explicitly define  $m_k$  to be the value such that  $\dfrac{4k}{4k-2}+2m_k+\dfrac{m_k}{2k(4k-2)}=1$ . Since  $\dfrac{4k}{4k-2}>1$ , it follows that  $m_k < 0$ . But this is really good because now both of our inequalities are satisfied. Thus, by choosing this certain  $m_k$  for all even  $k$ 's, we construct the sequence  $a_1, a_2, \ldots , a_{2010}$  such that  $a_1a_2>3, a_3a_4>7, \ldots , a_{2009}a_{2010} > 4019$  and the reverse inequality  $a_ia_j \le i+j$  for all other pairs  $i,j$ . Now all we need to do is decrease  $a_1, a_3, \ldots , a_{2009}$  so that the  $>$  signs all become  $=$  signs, and equality is achieved, so we are finally done.  $\Box$ Explicitly, my construction is:   $$ a_k=\left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
\sqrt{2k+\dfrac{1}{2k}}-C_k&\text{ if k is odd}
\sqrt{2k-\dfrac{4}{(4k-1)^2}}& \text{ if k is even}
\end{array}
\right. $$   for some constant  $C_k$  enough to change the  $>$  signs to  $=$  signs.</details>

