The solution from my textbook, which I apparently never posted (note that as written in post #6, the problem only works if  $M$  is on segments  $XY$  and  $BC$ ):

Let  $I_A$  be the center of the  $A$ -excircle, tangent to  $\overline{BC}$  at  $T$ , and to the extensions of  $\overline{AB}$  and  $\overline{AC}$  at  $U$  and  $V$ . We see that  $AU = AV = s = 2$ . Then  $\overline{XY}$  is the radical axis of the  $A$ -excircle and the circle of radius zero at  $A$ . Therefore  $AM = MT$ .

[asy]
size(12cm); pair A = dir(130); pair B = dir(190); pair C = dir(-10); pair I = incenter(A, B, C); pair L = dir(-90); pair I_A = 2*L-I;; pair T = foot(I_A, B, C); pair U = foot(I_A, A, B); pair V = foot(I_A, A, C); pair X = midpoint(A--U); pair Y = midpoint(A--V); pair M = extension(B, C, X, Y); filldraw(A--B--C--cycle, invisible, blue); draw(B--U, blue); draw(C--V, blue); draw(X--Y, blue); draw(A--M, deepgreen); draw(arc(I_A, abs(I_A-T), -10, 190), grey);
dot(" $A$ ", A, dir(A)); dot(" $B$ ", B, dir(150)); dot(" $C$ ", C, dir(30)); dot(" $I_A$ ", I_A, dir(I_A)); dot(" $T$ ", T, dir(90)); dot(" $U$ ", U, dir(135)); dot(" $V$ ", V, dir(45)); dot(" $X$ ", X, dir(X)); dot(" $Y$ ", Y, dir(Y)); dot(" $M$ ", M, dir(270));
/* -----------------------------------------------------------------+ |                 TSQX: by CJ Quines and Evan Chen                  | | https://github.com/vEnhance/dotfiles/blob/main/py-scripts/tsqx.py | +-------------------------------------------------------------------+ !size(12cm); A = dir 130 B 150 = dir 190 C 30 = dir -10 I := incenter A B C L := dir -90 I_A = 2*L-I; T 90 = foot I_A B C U 135 = foot I_A A B V 45 = foot I_A A C X = midpoint A--U Y = midpoint A--V M 270 = extension B C X Y A--B--C--cycle / 0.1 palecyan / blue B--U / blue C--V / blue X--Y / blue A--M / deepgreen !draw(arc(I_A, abs(I_A-T), -10, 190), grey); */
[/asy]
Assume without loss of generality that  $T$  lies on segment  $MC$ , as opposed to segment  $MB$ . Then \[ AB + BM + MA  = AB + BM + MT = AB + BT = AB + BU = AU = 2 \] as desired.

Define  $A',C',X,Y,Z\in(ABC)$  such that  $I_1=AA'\cap BX$ ,  $I_2=CC'\cap BZ$ , and  $M=BY\cap AC$ . ( $A',C',X,Z$  are suitably chosen midpoints of arcs  $BC,AB,AY,CY$ .)

WLOG  $(ABC)$  is the unit circle in the complex plane. It's easy to show that there exist complex numbers  $u,v,w$  such that  $a=u^2$ ,  $b=v^2$ ,  $c=w^2$ ,  $a'=-vw$ ,  $c'=-uv$ , and  $n=uw$ ; first we can change the signs of  $v,w$  as needed so that  $b'=-uw$  and  $c'=-uv$ , and then  $(a/c')(b/a')(c/b')=e^{\pi i}=-1\implies a'=-vw$ .

Furthermore, there exists some complex number  $r$  such that  $y=r^2$ ,  $x=ru$ , and  $z=-rw$ . Indeed, we must have  $x^2=ay$ ,  $z^2=cy$ , and  $\angle{XOZ}+\angle{A'OC'}=180^\circ$  (directed angles), so  $(z/x)(c'/a')=e^{\pi i}=-1\implies x/u=-z/w$  (then we can negate  $r$  if necessary).

First we find that
\begin{align*}
m=by\cap ac\implies y=r^2 &= \frac{u^2w^2(v^2-u^2-w^2)}{v^2(u^2+w^2)-2u^2w^2} 
i_1=aa'\cap bx\implies i_1 &= v^2+\frac{r(u-v)(u+v)(v+w)}{vr+uw} 
i_2=cc'\cap bz\implies i_2 &= v^2+\frac{r(w-v)(u+v)(v+w)}{vr-uw}.
\end{align*}Now notice that  $B=I_1X\cap I_2Z$ , so because  $BNZX$  is cyclic, spiral similarity yields that  $BNI_2I_1$  is cyclic iff  $\triangle{NI_1I_2}\sim\triangle{NXZ}$ . But it's easy to verify that
\[\frac{n-i_1}{n-i_2}=\frac{n-x}{n-z} \Longleftrightarrow r^2=\frac{u^2w^2(v^2-u^2-w^2)}{v^2(u^2+w^2)-2u^2w^2},\]as desired.

Select a point  $P$  on  $\overrightarrow{MB}$  with  $MA = MP = MC$ . Then 
\[\text{Pow}(M, \odot(BI_1A)) = MA \cdot MB = MP \cdot MB,\]
so  $AI_1PB$  is cyclic. Similarly  $CI_2PB$  is cyclic, and  $I_1$  and  $I_2$  are the arc midpoints in these circles.

[asy]
unitsize(100);
pair B, A, C, M, I, I1, I2, P, N;
B = dir(110); A = dir(220); C = dir(320);
M = (A + C)/2; I1 = incenter(B, M, A); I2 = incenter(B, M, C); I = incenter(A, B, C); N = -circumcenter(A, I, C);
P = M + abs(A-M) * dir(B - M);
draw(incircle(B, A, M)^^incircle(B, C, M), gray(0.8));
draw(M--P^^A--C, gray(0.8));
draw(unitcircle^^arc(circumcenter(B, I1, A), A, B)^^arc(circumcenter(B, I2, C), B, C), cyan);
add(pathticks(A--I1, 1, 0.5, 1, 3, magenta)); add(pathticks(I1--P, 1, 0.5, 1, 3, magenta));
add(pathticks(C--I2, 2, 0.5, 1, 3, magenta)); add(pathticks(I2--P, 2, 0.5, 1, 3, magenta));
add(pathticks(A--N, 3, 0.5, 1, 3, magenta)); add(pathticks(N--C, 3, 0.5, 1, 3, magenta));
draw(B--I1^^B--I2^^B--N, rgb(0, 0.6, 0.6));
draw(A--I1--P--I2--C--N--cycle, heavymagenta);
draw(B--A^^B--C^^B--P, gray(0.4));
draw(circumcircle(I1, I2, N), dotted);

dot(B^^A^^C^^I1^^I2^^N^^P);

label(" $B$ ", B, dir(B));
label(" $A$ ", A, dir(A));
