Invert at  $B$ . Then  $I_1^{*}$ ,  $I_2^{*}$ ,  $N^{*}$  are the internal, internal, external bisector feet from  $\angle A^{*}BP^{*}$ ,  $\angle C^{*}BP^{*}$ ,  $\angle A^{*}BC^{*}$  to the respective sides of  $\triangle A^{*}P^{*}C^{*}$ . By Menelaus  $I_1^{*}I_2^{*}N^{*}$  are collinear so  $BI_1I_2N$  is cyclic, as desired.

