*Proof.* Angle chasing, we have  $$ \measuredangle DMA+\measuredangle ABM=\measuredangle DP_cA+\measuredangle P_cEM=\measuredangle DEP_c+\measuredangle P_cEM=\measuredangle DEM, $$  as desired.**Claim 6.**  $(ABC)$  is tangent to  $(DEF)$ .

*Proof.* Let  $N$  be point on the tangent to  $(DEF)$  at  $M$ . Then  $(ABC)$  and  $(DEF)$  are tangent iff  $MN$  is tangent to  $(ABC)$  iff  $\measuredangle AMN=\measuredangle ABM$ , or equivalently  $$ \measuredangle DEM=\measuredangle DMN=\measuredangle DMA+\measuredangle AMN=\measuredangle DMA+\measuredangle ABM, $$  which is true, so we are done.

