We will assume the above configuration, the others can be handled simalarly (I could do the whole thing out with directed lengths but this is easier). Let  $\omega_i=(A_{i+1}A_{i+2}A_{i+3})$ . Let  $\mathcal{P}$  be the statement that
\[\sum_i\frac{1}{OA_i^2-r_i^2}=0.\]
Note that  $OA_i^2-r_i^2$  is the power of  $A_i$  with respect to  $\omega_i$ , so in our configuration, we want to show that
\[\frac{1}{AE\cdot AC}+\frac{1}{CA\cdot CF} = \frac{1}{BG\cdot BD}+\frac{1}{DH\cdot DB}.\]
Thus,
\[\mathcal{P}\iff \frac{1}{AC}\left(\frac{1}{AC}+\frac{1}{CF}\right) = \frac{1}{BD}\left(\frac{1}{BG}+\frac{1}{DH}\right).\]
Let  $I=AC\cap BD$ . Then power of a point on  $I$  tells us that
\[IA\cdot IC = IG\cdot ID = IH\cdot IB =: \alpha\]
and
\[IB\cdot ID = IE\cdot IC = IF\cdot IA =: \beta.\]
Therefore,
\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{AC}\left(\frac{1}{AE}+\frac{1}{CF}\right) &= \frac{1}{IA+IC}\left(\frac{1}{IE-IA}+\frac{1}{IF-IC}\right) 
&= \frac{1}{IA+IC}\left(\frac{1}{\beta/IC-IA}+\frac{1}{\beta/IA-IC}\right) 
&= \frac{1}{\beta-\alpha}
\end{align*}
and
\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{BD}\left(\frac{1}{BG}+\frac{1}{DH}\right) &= \frac{1}{IB+ID}\left(\frac{1}{IB-IG}+\frac{1}{ID-IH}\right) 
&= \frac{1}{IB+ID}\left(\frac{1}{IB-\alpha/ID}+\frac{1}{ID-\alpha/IB}\right) 
&= \frac{1}{\beta-\alpha},
\end{align*}
so the truth of  $\mathcal{P}$  is verified, as desired.

