Let  $X = (AEFI) \cap (BDGI)$ . First, because 
\begin{align*}
\measuredangle PFX &= \measuredangle PFG + \measuredangle GFX
&= \measuredangle ABI + \measuredangle EIX  
&= \measuredangle ABI + \measuredangle EID + \measuredangle DIX 
&= \measuredangle IAB + \measuredangle DIX 
&= \measuredangle PGX,
\end{align*}
we have that  $X$  lies on  $(PFG)$ . Moreover,  $\measuredangle FXP = \measuredangle FGP = \measuredangle FEI = \measuredangle FXI$ , so  $P,X,I$  collinear.

Finally, let lines  $EA$  and  $DB$  meet at  $Y$ . Then because  $X$  is the Miquel point of  $ADBE$ , we have  $X,I,Y$  collinear. In addition,  $K$  lies on the polar of  $\overline{AB} \cap \overline{DE}$ , so  $I,K,Y$  are collinear by Brokard's theorem. Thus,  $P,K,Y$  are collinear, as desired.

