& \measuredangle FNG= \measuredangle FNI+ \measuredangle ING= \measuredangle FAI+ \measuredangle IBG= \frac{1}{2}(\measuredangle B+\measuredangle A)
\end{align*}
and finally  $$ \measuredangle FNP=\measuredangle FGP= \measuredangle DGY= \measuredangle DBY= \measuredangle BAI= \measuredangle FAI= \measuredangle INF \implies \overline{I-N-P} $$  So  $\overline{R-K-I-N-P}$  and   $AE,BD$  and  $KP$  are concurrent or parallel.

