stem_md:
How many ordered pairs of positive integers  $(m, n)$  satisfy the system

\begin{align*}
\gcd (m^3, n^2) & = 2^2 \cdot 3^2,
 \text{LCM} [m^2, n^3] & = 2^4 \cdot 3^4 \cdot 5^6,
\end{align*}

where  $\gcd(a, b)$  and  $\text{LCM}[a, b]$  denote the greatest common divisor and least common multiple of  $a$  and  $b$ , respectively?

solution_md:
We compute the sum without the former condition, and then subtract one and divide by  $2$ . Thus, let \[S_n = \sum_{\substack{a+b >n\gcd(a, b) = 1}}\dfrac{1}{ab}.\] Then:
\begin{align*}
S_{n+1}-S_n &= \sum_{\substack{a+b >n+1\gcd(a, b) = 1a, b\le n+1}}\dfrac{1}{ab} - \sum_{\substack{a+b >n\gcd(a, b) = 1a,b\le n}}\dfrac{1}{ab} 
&= \sum_{\substack{a+b >n+1\gcd(a, b) = 1a, b\le n}}\dfrac{1}{ab} + \sum_{\substack{a+b >n+1\gcd(a, b) = 1a = n+1}}\dfrac{1}{ab} + \sum_{\substack{a+b >n+1\gcd(a, b) = 1b = n+1}}\dfrac{1}{ab} - \sum_{\substack{a+b =n+1\gcd(a, b) = 1a,b\le n}}\dfrac{1}{ab} - \sum_{\substack{a+b >n+1\gcd(a, b) = 1a,b\le n}}\dfrac{1}{ab} 
&= 2\sum_{\substack{a+b >n+1\gcd(a, b) = 1a = n+1}}\dfrac{1}{ab} - \sum_{\substack{a+b =n+1\gcd(a, b) = 1a,b\le n}}\dfrac{1}{ab} 
&= \sum_{\gcd(a, n+1) = 1}\dfrac{2}{a(n+1)} - \sum_{\gcd(a, n+1) = 1}\dfrac{1}{a(n-a+1)} 
&= \sum_{\gcd(a, n+1) = 1}\dfrac{2(n-a+1)-(n+1)}{a(n+1)(n-a+1)} 
&= \dfrac{1}{n+1}\sum_{\gcd(a, n+1) = 1}\dfrac{(n-a+1)-a}{a(n-a+1)} 
&= \dfrac{1}{n+1}\sum_{\gcd(a, n+1) = 1}\dfrac{1}{a}-\dfrac{1}{n-a+1} 
&= 0.
\end{align*}
Hence, the  $S_n$  is constant, and calculating  $S_2 = 2$ , we find the required conclusion.  $\square$

candidates:
Let  $A_n$  be the desired sum.  Remark that  $A_1 = \tfrac{1}{2}$  and  \begin{align*}
		A_{n} - A_{n-1} &= \sum_{\substack{\gcd(a,n) = 1,  a < n}} \frac{1}{na} - \sum_{\substack{a+b=n, a<b  \gcd(a,b) = 1}} \frac{1}{ab} 
		&= \frac{1}{n} \sum_{\substack{\gcd(a,n) = 1,  a < n}} \frac{1}{a} - \sum_{\substack{\gcd(a,n) = 1  a \le n/2}} \frac{1}{a(n-a)} 
		&= \frac{1}{n} \sum_{\substack{\gcd(a,n) = 1,  a < n}} \frac{1}{a} - \frac{1}{n} \sum_{\substack{\gcd(a,n) = 1  a \le n/2}} \left( \frac{1}{a} + \frac{1}{n-a} \right) 
		&= \frac{1}{n} \sum_{\substack{\gcd(a,n) = 1,  a < n}} \frac{1}{a} - \frac{1}{n} \sum_{\substack{\gcd(a,n) = 1  a \le n}} \frac{1}{a} 
		&= 0.
	\end{align*}

